  "story": {
    "day": 173,
    "title": "A Rainy Evening at Home",
    "sentences": [
      "It was the fourth rainy day that week, so Kaya stayed inside.",
      "She looked forward to going skiing with her cousins the next morning.",
      "First, Kaya helped her little sister draw a horse and a zebra.",
      "Next, they added a dolphin and an octopus to the colorful picture.",
      "Then Kaya went to the kitchen and cooked tomato spaghetti for dinner.",
      "She also made a fresh salad with sweet corn and green cabbage.",
      "Her dad cooked pork and potato curry earlier that afternoon.",
      "Mom came into the kitchen and smiled at the warm food.",
      "\"I'll heat the curry, so we'll eat soon, and you'll love it, won't you?\"",
      "Suddenly, Kaya heard the phone ring, and Mom spoke with Aunt Yumi.",
      "\"They'll ski, she'll join us, and you mustn't worry because Dad will drive.\"",
      "Finally, they shared cake for dessert, and it was certainly a wonderful evening."
    ]
  }
}